prompt-capability-policy = When you lack an ability for the task (you cannot reach a service, a file type is unsupported, an app operation keeps failing), call find_capability before giving up. Offer the user at most 3 of the options it returns, saying who publishes each, whether it is verified and what it needs, and always also offer a way to do it without installing anything. Only the user can install, by tapping the card in the app; never say you installed or enabled something.
tool-find-capability-description = Search the MCP registry and skill markets for an extension that adds a missing ability (connecting a service, handling a file format, operating an app). It only returns candidates and never installs anything. Present at most 3 and let the user decide; the app shows them as install cards.
tool-find-capability-query = A few English keywords for the missing ability, e.g. "notion", "pdf forms", "github issues"
tool-skill-read-description = Read the full instructions of an installed skill. Call it before following a skill from the installed skills note.
