tool-floorplan-save-description = Call when the user sends a floor plan photo, or describes room sizes (like "living room 6 by 4.5 meters"), and wants help with the layout or renovation (never only describe the plan in text): saves the rooms as a floor plan, and a floor plan card shows under your reply that opens the plan, furniture and size views and lets the user check sizes one by one. From a drawing, read each room's name, position and size, in meters (origin at the top left, x to the right, y down; the top of the drawing is north unless it has a compass); shared walls must line up. Never invent a precise number for a size that is unreadable, hidden or not labeled: estimate it from the scale, draw that, and also list it in unclear with which wall and why, so the user can measure it. When the user is only describing rooms, don't draw the ones they haven't mentioned. Furnish each room for the household, with one or two sentences of advice and a few one-tap ideas. If this conversation already has a floor plan, change it with floorplan_edit instead of saving again. When the user wants a renovation schedule, make a plan with plan in this conversation; it shows in the floor plan's Progress tab.
tool-floorplan-edit-description = Change this conversation's floor plan: when the user says "move the sofa to the east wall", "add a bookshelf wall", "the main bedroom's east wall is 3.75 m", or taps a room idea. Each call makes a new version of the current scheme (the user can compare and go back); when the user wants another scheme (like "also try one with the dining and living rooms opened up"), set new_scheme to copy the current scheme into B, C… and change that. Put only the rooms that change in rooms, matched by name, with only the fields that change (furniture alone replaces just the furniture); when renaming, put the old name in was. When the user measures an unclear size, fill it in measured by its label; the room stretches to the measured value. Afterwards say only a sentence or two about what changed.
tool-floorplan-x = X in meters, growing to the right.
tool-floorplan-y = Y in meters, growing downward.
tool-floorplan-w = Width (along x) in meters.
tool-floorplan-h = Depth (along y) in meters.
tool-floorplan-rect = A rectangular room's position and size (top-left x, y plus width w and depth h, in meters). Use points for irregular rooms.
tool-floorplan-points = An irregular room's polygon corners [[x, y], ...] in order, in meters.
tool-floorplan-rotation = Rotation around the center in degrees, usually 0 or 90.
tool-floorplan-item-name = Furniture name, like "3-seat sofa", "1.8 m bed", "dining table", "wardrobe".
tool-floorplan-room-name = Room name, like "Living room", "Main bedroom", "Bathroom"; unique within the plan.
tool-floorplan-facing = Which way the room's main light comes from.
tool-floorplan-openings = Doors and windows: each is a stretch of wall (x1, y1 to x2, y2), kind door or window.
tool-floorplan-furniture = Furniture, positioned and sized in meters, inside the room with walkways left clear.
tool-floorplan-advice = One or two sentences of advice for this room with the reason, like "Light comes from the south; the sofa is steadiest against the north wall."
tool-floorplan-ideas = Two or three changes the user can ask for with one tap, a few words each, like "Sofa to east wall", "Add a bookshelf wall".
tool-floorplan-was = The room's old name, when renaming it.
tool-floorplan-unclear = Sizes that are unreadable on the drawing and need measuring. Each is a stretch of wall (x1, y1 to x2, y2) with a length estimated from the scale.
tool-floorplan-unclear-room = Which room the wall belongs to (room name).
tool-floorplan-unclear-label = A short name for this size, like "Main bedroom east wall", "Bathroom length".
tool-floorplan-unclear-estimate = Length estimated from the scale, in meters.
tool-floorplan-unclear-note = One sentence on why it is unclear and what depends on it, like "A watermark covers the number; the wardrobe and bed sizes depend on it."
tool-floorplan-title = The plan's name, like "New home".
tool-floorplan-kind = Bedrooms and living rooms, like "3 bed, 1 living".
tool-floorplan-area = Floor area labeled on the drawing in square meters; leave out if not labeled.
tool-floorplan-rooms = All rooms.
tool-floorplan-note = What this version changes, one short sentence, like "Sofa moved to the east wall".
tool-floorplan-new-scheme = When true, make a new scheme instead of a new version of the current one.
tool-floorplan-scheme = Which scheme to start from (A, B…); the current one when left out.
