tool-save-trip-costs = Cost breakdown in five groups: transport (getting there and around), stay, tickets, food and other. Each group has one or more lines and every line names its source. Fill it in whenever you plan a trip; if the user stated a budget put it in budget, and if the plan is over it give concrete ways to save in savings.
tool-save-trip-cost-lines = Lines, one price each, such as "return train", "Lingyin Temple tickets", "meals for 3 people, 3 days". When there are stay options, put the stay in stays instead of here
tool-save-trip-cost-category = Group: transport, stay, tickets, food or other
tool-save-trip-stays = Places to stay, 2 or 3 picked along the route, each with a price and its source; put the nightly price in unit_amount and the nights in quantity
tool-save-trip-stay-name = Name of the place, searchable on a map
tool-save-trip-stay-note = One line on how it suits the group and getting around, such as "family rooms" or "2 metro stops to the lake"
tool-save-trip-stay-chosen = true for the one you recommend; only one
tool-save-trip-people = How many people in total, for the per-person figure
tool-save-trip-budget = The total budget the user actually said, in yuan; for "under 3000" put 3000. Leave it out if they did not say one
tool-save-trip-savings = Ways to save when over budget, each concrete, such as which place to stay instead or what to swap for something free
tool-save-trip-saving-title = The change in one line, such as "Stay near Longxiangqiao station"
tool-save-trip-saving-detail = One line on why or the trade-off, such as "a 6-year-old can walk the 2.8 km"
tool-save-trip-saving-saves = How much it saves in yuan, worked out from the sourced prices above
tool-price-label = What this is, such as "return train" or "lakeside family room"
tool-price-amount = Total in yuan. Only work it out from prices you really saw in the source; leave it out if you found none
tool-price-unit-amount = Unit price in yuan, such as per night, per ticket or per person; exactly the number the source shows
tool-price-quantity = How many, such as nights or tickets; with a unit price and quantity the total is worked out for you
tool-price-per = Unit for the unit price, such as "night", "ticket" or "person"
tool-price-source = Where the price came from: web, a page found by searching in this reply; app, a screen you read in an app in this reply; estimate, only for things that can only be estimated, with a basis; none, not found, amount left empty
tool-price-url = Required for web: the page link, which must be one web_search or read_page returned in this reply
tool-price-site = For web: the site name, such as "Lingyin Temple official site"
tool-price-app = Required for app: the app where you read the price, such as "Trip.com" or "12306"
tool-price-basis = Required for estimate: how it was estimated, such as "average spend from several Dianping listings"
tool-price-reason = For none: why it was not found, such as "no price online for Nov 14–16"
tool-price-applies-to = Which date the price is for, such as "Nov 14" or "check-in Nov 14–16"
tool-check-price-description = Call this when the web has no price for the actual dates (common for hotels, flights and trains). The chat shows a card asking whether to check it in an app on the phone. Once the user taps Check, you may only look at prices in that app: search, pick dates and the number of people, read prices. Sign-in, booking, ordering and payment buttons are blocked and personal-detail fields cannot be filled. Call note_app_price for each price you read. If the user says no, leave that price empty for them to fill in. Find the app with find_apps first.
tool-check-price-app = App id returned by find_apps
tool-check-price-name = App name, such as "Trip.com"
tool-check-price-item = What to check, a few words, such as "stay" or "train tickets"
tool-check-price-detail = Note for the user: why the web had no price, how you will search and how many you will note, such as "No price online for Nov 14–16. Xiaoban will open Trip.com, search family rooms near West Lake for those dates and 3 people, and note the first 3 prices."
tool-check-price-wanted = How many to note, 3 by default
tool-note-price-description = While checking prices, call this once for every price you read on screen; it is noted and the progress updates. The amount must match the number on screen exactly or it is refused.
tool-note-price-label = Which place or item, such as "lakeside family hotel"
tool-note-price-amount = Amount shown on screen, in yuan
tool-trip-expense-description = Call this on a trip when the user says they spent money (such as "lunch was 126" or "taxi 32"). It goes into the expense log, filed under this trip. Only use it when this conversation already has a trip.
tool-trip-expense-amount = Amount in yuan
tool-trip-expense-name = What it was for, a few words, such as "Lunch · Zhiweiguan"
