tool-propose-schedule-description = Call this when the user wants you to do something automatically at a set time, on a regular schedule or every so often ("every morning at 8, look up yesterday's AI news", "check where this parcel is every 2 hours", "every evening at 9, check whether it will rain tomorrow"). It shows a task card under your reply; nothing runs until the user taps "Start" on it. If the time is unclear, ask first and never guess. Write task as complete instructions to yourself: each run only sees that text, so include what to look up, how to pick, and what the result should look like. Repeats run at most every 30 minutes and can be limited to a time window; to watch for something to happen (parcel delivered, a price dropping to some level) fill in condition and the task stops once it is met. It is only a proposal: do not say it is set up, and do not list the card's details again in your reply. One card per reply.
tool-propose-schedule-title = A short name for the task, like "AI news brief" or "Watch parcel SF1234"
tool-propose-schedule-task = What to do on each run, as complete instructions, like "Search yesterday's AI news, pick the 5 most important, one sentence and a link each"
