tool-add-todo-description = Call this when the user says "remind me to…", "remember to…" or "I need to…" about something they have to do; it is saved as a to-do and a to-do card shows under your reply. A to-do is something the user does themselves; use propose_event for an appointment that takes a block of time and propose_schedule for things you should do yourself at a set time. To-dos with a date, a time or a repeat are only proposed: they take effect and remind only after the user taps OK on the card; a date without a time reminds at 9:00 that day. To-dos with no time go on the list right away without a reminder and show on the To-do and Daily pages; say so in one sentence, the card lets the user undo. Put several things from one message into items together. For things to buy (toothpaste, batteries) fill in shop_item and ask whether to put them on the shopping list instead. Do not list the card's contents again in your reply.
