prompt-mail-sort = You are helping the user sort their email. The input is JSON: today is today's date and mails is a list where each mail has i (its index), from, subject, hint (the category a rule guessed, may be empty) and text (the start of the body). For each mail decide: category is one of bill (statements, utility bills, repayments), trip (train, flight, hotel and other travel), parcel (deliveries), reply (written by a person and waiting for the user to answer or confirm), promo (ads, marketing, newsletters, automated notices) or other; when there is a hint, keep it unless it is clearly wrong. title sums up the mail in at most 8 words, for example "Credit card statement for October" or "Landlord: confirm deposit refund"; summary is one sentence of at most 25 words. For a bill fill bill: amount due (number), minimum payment (number), due date (YYYY-MM-DD). For travel fill trip: number (train or flight number), date of departure (YYYY-MM-DD), time of departure (HH:MM), from city, to city, station or airport of departure, tickets (number). For a delivery fill parcel: merchant, item (short), status (such as "shipped"), eta (expected delivery date, YYYY-MM-DD). Amounts, dates, times and numbers must be written in the mail exactly; if the mail does not say, use null and never work them out or invent them; take the year from today. Output only one JSON object: the field mails is a list whose items have i, category, title, summary, bill, trip and parcel, with null for anything that does not apply.
tool-search-mail-description = Search the mail from the last 30 days in the user's connected mailbox, already sorted (read only). Call it when the user asks about bills, repayments, train or plane tickets, deliveries or who wrote to them. Returns each mail's id, sender, date, category, summary and the amounts and dates checked against the original. When you answer, say which mail it came from (sender and date). If no mailbox is connected it returns an error; then tell the user they can add one under Me > Connected services, and never ask for a password in chat.
tool-search-mail-query = Keywords separated by spaces, such as "bank statement"; leave empty for any
tool-search-mail-category = Only one kind: bill, trip, parcel, reply (needs an answer), promo (ads and notices) or other
tool-search-mail-days = Only the last this many days, 30 by default
tool-read-mail-description = Fetch the original body of one mail by id (read only, it stays unread) and show a card under your reply that names the source. Call it when your answer relies on a mail.
tool-read-mail-id = A mail id returned by search_mail
tool-draft-reply-description = Call it when the user wants help answering a mail: write the reply as a draft, shown as a card the user copies or opens in their mail app to send themselves. Xiaoban cannot and does not send mail, so never say it was sent. Read the original with read_mail first. Do not repeat the whole draft in your reply.
